{"ref":"BDB, יְהוֹיָרִיב","hw":"יְהוֹיָרִיב","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יְהוֹיָרִיב</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹיָרִיב</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m.</strong> 𝔊 Ἰωιαρειβ, Ἰωαρειβ, Ἰωαρειμ, etc. <strong>(</strong><span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <em>pleadeth</em>, or <em>contendeth</em><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  name of a priestly family <span dir=\"rtl\">יְהוֹ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:10\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.10\">1 Ch 9:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 24:7\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.24.7\">24:7</a>; = <span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 11:10\" href=\"/Nehemiah.11.10\">Ne 11:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:6\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.6\">12:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:19\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.19\">19</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  teacher in Ezra’s time <a data-ref=\"Ezra 8:16\" href=\"/Ezra.8.16\">Ezr 8:16</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  a Judaite <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 11:5\" href=\"/Nehemiah.11.5\">Ne 11:5</a>.","next":"BDB, יְהוּכַל","prev":"BDB, יְהוֹיָקִים"}